<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kachin State</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kachin State is the northernmost state of Myanmar, bordering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, with its capital at Myitkyina. Its mountains and the upper Irrawaddy valley are home to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kachin-people">Kachin peoples</a> and to Shan and Burman communities, and it includes the jade mines of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hpakant">Hpakant</a>. It was formed in 1948 and has been a centre of armed conflict between the Kachin Independence Army and the Burmese military since the 1960s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kachin-state.jpg" alt="Kachin State" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Saimawnkham · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Moengkaung.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
